Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: mark the camera front-facing

This unit has only the user-facing module fitted (the rear module is not
populated -- see #70), so orientation = 0 is a fact about the hardware.

"rotation" is deliberately NOT set. It has never been measured on this
device, and a wrong value silently turns every captured image upside down in
anything that honours it. Absent, no control is created and consumers default
to 0 -- the same result, without the false claim.

Rebuilt clean, and `make CHECK_DTBS=y` still reports 0 warnings.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -2752,6 +2752,20 @@
 		reset-gpios = <&pio 33 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		powerdown-gpios = <&pio 29 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
+		/*
+		 * 0 = front. This unit has only the user-facing module fitted
+		 * (see #70), so this is a fact about the hardware, not a guess.
+		 * libcamera requires V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION and complains
+		 * that "the sensor kernel driver needs to be fixed" without it.
+		 *
+		 * "rotation" is deliberately NOT set. It has never been
+		 * measured on this device, and a wrong value silently turns
+		 * every captured image upside down in anything that honours it.
+		 * Absent, no control is created and consumers default to 0,
+		 * which is the same result without the false claim.
+		 */
+		orientation = <0>;
+
 		port {
 			hi556_out: endpoint {
 				remote-endpoint = <&cam_bridge_in>;
